  "metadata": {
    "sources": [
      "https://www.nagraaudio.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/Nagra-HD-PREAMP-User-Manual-English.pdf",
      "https://www.hifinews.com/content/nagra-hd-preamp-preamplifier"
    ],
    "verified": false,
    "protocolFamily": "nagra-ascii",
    "notes": "Two-box tube line stage. Both control paths are documented in the owner's manual: ASCII commands terminated with a carriage return on the power supply chassis SUB-D9, and Philips RC-5 infrared on device group 16. One trap dominates any installation: a jack plugged into the REMOTE IN socket takes priority over BOTH infrared and RS-232, and the manual states the remote's on/off key stops working in that case — so a working serial link can still appear to ignore power commands. Volume is relay-switched transformer taps in 0.5 dB steps, not a continuous control, and the unit self-mutes for about 2.5 minutes from cold while the tubes warm. Nagra Customer Care (Aug 2026) confirmed the RS-232 section and pinning diagram are on page 28 of the official manual; the public PDF's pin graphic did not OCR — cable type remains unknown until verified on hardware."
  }
